{
  "version": 4,
  "product": "SESCCO MS",
  "principles": {
    "archive": "Archive is a reversible lifecycle boundary. For parent masters, operational child scope may inherit the archive state without rewriting permanent child/history rows.",
    "delete_unused": "For selected operational masters, Delete means a 30-day reversible soft-delete. Parent masters soft-delete their owned/current child masters into the same recovery window while protected workflow/audit history remains immutable.",
    "workflow": "Operational transactions are closed, cancelled, reversed, released or superseded through their workflow; they are not archived/deleted as masters.",
    "immutable": "Audit, movement and finalized-document evidence is append-only or reversal-based and must never expose ordinary delete/archive actions.",
    "access": "System users and memberships are deactivated/reactivated so audit actor history remains resolvable.",
    "trash": "Delete recovery is distinct from Archive. Deleted masters and cascade-owned child masters are hidden from active selectors and recoverable for 30 days. Cascade recovery metadata ensures parent restore revives only children deleted by that parent operation.",
    "cascade": "Branch/Office and Department soft-delete their current employee masters; Manpower Supplier soft-deletes its worker masters; Project soft-deletes its project inventory location/stock masters. All cascade-owned children share the parent 30-day window and restore atomically with the parent. Independently deleted children are not resurrected."
  },
